{
  "abstract": "An independent Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization resolving Sanders' Question 5.1 (Ben Green's Open Problem 51 at density 1/2), following the proof of Jensen Kohlmeyer and Liam Kruer (2026). The compared declaration matches `Green51.green_51.one_half` verbatim from google-deepmind/formal-conjectures: for every k > 0, there exists a constant c : Nat such that for all sufficiently large n and every A subset F_2^n of density alpha > 1/2 - k / sqrt(n), the sumset A + A contains an affine coset of dimension at least n - c (codimension at most c). As a proof-level intermediate step inside `Solution.lean` (not stated in the compared theorem's type), the proof constructs a linear subspace of codimension at most ceil(1 + 256 * e * k^2).",
